mtmd: take upstream's helper and tokenize signatures

The app's Swift code is shared with the main llama.cpp pin, whose mtmd passes a
`mtmd_helper_init_opt` to `mtmd_helper_bitmap_init_from_file` and takes
`mtmd_tokenize`'s bitmaps as `const mtmd_bitmap * const *`. This fork predates
both, so the app does not compile against it. Adds the options struct (unused) and
its default, and the const signature; the fork's own callers follow.

Applied at build time by ios/build-llama.sh for vendor/llamacpp-prismml only. Remove
once the fork carries upstream's signatures.
---
diff --git a/tools/mtmd/mtmd-cli.cpp b/tools/mtmd/mtmd-cli.cpp
index f6c787f..32cacf9 100644
--- a/tools/mtmd/mtmd-cli.cpp
+++ b/tools/mtmd/mtmd-cli.cpp
@@ -184,7 +184,7 @@ struct mtmd_cli_context {
     }
 
     bool load_media(const std::string & fname) {
-        auto res = mtmd_helper_bitmap_init_from_file(ctx_vision.get(), fname.c_str(), false);
+        auto res = mtmd_helper_bitmap_init_from_file(ctx_vision.get(), fname.c_str(), false, mtmd_helper_init_opt_default());
         if (!res.bitmap) {
             return false;
         }
